# Cubeless solar occlusion

The HDR solar disc could remain visible inside the rebaked cloud masses because
the existing coverage-to-extinction ramp only reached full occlusion at 0.65.
The owned `M_Cubeless_Clouds_Fog` now reaches full occlusion at 0.35, using a
continuous 0.015–0.35 ramp. Clear sky still reveals the disc and thin edges retain
gradual transmission. No circular sun mask or additional texture fetch is added.

The premultiplied backdrop compensation remains unchanged, preserving the cloud
colour/sky mixture as extinction increases. The existing solar-visibility weight
keeps the deep-night opacity path unchanged. Light shafts, sun intensity, cloud
textures, animation settings and source VDB layout are not changed.

The visual comparison holds cloud-MID motion at 60 seconds without changing the
actor's animation controls. The old shader leaves a white point at the centre;
the adjusted shader hides it. Separate poses show dense coverage and clear-sky
visibility. Temporary MID overrides are restored through the normal `UpdateSky`.

Validation passed: complete offline full profile (42 checks), native cold load
and affected-map Windows SM6 cook with UnrealMCP disabled. The 1001-point blend
check confirms monotonic extinction and unchanged smooth-background composition.
After PIE ended, the material was saved and the temporary MID overrides were
restored (`UseLiveTime=1`, `MotionTime=0`). The user's current time was preserved.

